  I’d avoid saying “high signal lecture” directly on every thumbnail. Better as a small recurring badge:
  HIGH SIGNAL CUT
  or
  DENSE LECTURE
  or
  NO FLUFF VERSION

  Main title should be the concept, not the format.

  Could automate this decently:

  1. Search image query from title keywords.
  2. Download top 3 candidates.
  3. Pick one manually or heuristically.
  4. Generate thumbnail with fixed template using PIL/ImageMagick.
  5. Store source URL in metadata for attribution.

  For now, I’d make 3 reusable templates:

  - diagram-left-title-right
  - full-bleed-image-dark-overlay
  - archival-paper-clean-label

  That gets you 80% of the look without AI slop.


